# flickos-layouts 1.83~test3: FloatingDefault=, the islands without a setting;
# flick-tiler 1.11: joins them into one panel under a full window; sfwbar
# +flickos7, as Footprint's dock; arc-theme and numix-icon-theme-circle: the
# GTK theme and the icons Tortuga names, already in FlickOS.
Depends: flickos-layouts (>= 1.83~test3),
         flick-tiler (>= 1.11~),
         sfwbar (>= 1.0~beta17+git20260910+flickos7),
         arc-theme,
         numix-icon-theme-circle,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Tortuga style and layout for the FlickOS desktop
 A dark style for FlickOS: slate title bars with thin buttons that get a
 round face under the pointer, a lantern copper accent, a deep slate
 terminal, and an island harbour at dusk on the wallpaper, with lanterns
 along the quay and their light in the water.
 .
 Its layout has three floating islands at the top with the apps button, the
 clock and the status, and a dock at the bottom with the desktops as a
 two-by-two grid beside it. While a window fills the screen the islands join
 into one panel and the dock hides.
 .
 Installing it adds Tortuga to Desktop Layout & Style; Software's Use sets
 the style and the layout together.
